  "intro": {
    "cards": [
      {
        "title": "The same rule, new places",
        "body": "The verb still fits the subject: **he works / they work**. Now the rule appears in **questions**, **negatives**, **was / were**, **there is / are**, and with words like **everybody**.",
        "points": [
          "Same idea: the verb must fit the subject",
          "Questions and negatives use **do / does** (or **don't / doesn't**)",
          "Some words look plural but take a **singular** verb"
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "do / does",
        "table": {
          "headers": [
            "Subject",
            "Question / negative"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "I / you / we / they",
              "Do they work? · They don't work."
            ],
            [
              "he / she / it",
              "Does he work? · She doesn't work."
            ]
          ]
        },
        "points": [
          "After do/does, use the **base** verb: Does he **work**? (not works)",
          "Avoid: *Do he work?* · *She don't like…*"
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "was / were · there is / are",
        "table": {
          "headers": [
            "Use",
            "Example"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "was",
              "He was late. · There was a problem."
            ],
            [
              "were",
              "They were late. · You were late. · There were problems."
            ]
          ]
        },
        "points": [
          "we → **were** (not was) · you → **were** (not was)",
          "there is + singular · there are + plural"
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "everybody / someone / nobody",
        "points": [
          "These usually take a **singular** verb: Everybody **likes**… · Someone **has**…",
          "Does everybody understand? (not Do everybody…)",
          "one of my friends **lives**… · each student **has**…"
        ],
        "table": {
          "headers": [
            "Avoid",
            "Say"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Everybody **like** weekends.",
              "Everybody **likes** weekends."
            ],
            [
              "Someone **have** my keys.",
              "Someone **has** my keys."
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "title": "Quick check",
        "points": [
          "____ he work here? → **Does**",
          "They ____ like fish. → **don't**",
          "There ____ two books. → **are**",
          "Everybody ____ weekends. → **likes**"
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
